{"public_message": "Sarah, fair question. Marcus's answer landed well with me. He answered what I asked directly and gave specifics rather than a polished dodge, and that part read as genuine.

The vote is where I hesitate. I did say I'd take note of early confident accusations, and Emily's right that this is the only one so far. But taking note isn't a conviction. A money holder in round one has every reason to blend in, and being the first to plant a flag on someone is the opposite of that. To me that looks more like someone playing hard than someone hiding. The same caution applies to the rest of us: Marcus is now the easy vote, and an easy consensus in round one is exactly the cover a holder would want.

So two questions before I commit. Marcus, Jordan's question is the right one: what in Arvin's actual words, not his timing, made him your pick? Arvin, Marcus asked you for a name. You don't owe him one, but if you had to vote right now, who would it be and why? How each of you answers will tell me more than anything so far.", "private_message_to": "Emily Carter", "private_message": "Emily, thanks for checking in. It partly tracks: the early vote is the one thing that stands out so far, and you caught the mismatch with his own list. My hesitation is that someone actually holding the money rarely makes himself the loudest person in round one. So I'm leaning the same way but not locked in, and I want to hear how he answers Jordan first. If he gets defensive or shifts his reasoning, I'm with you. Who's your second look if Marcus comes across clean?", "notes_update": "R1 cont: Marcus cast the first declared vote (Arvin), reasoning that Arvin hadn't named anyone. Emily pounced publicly on Marcus (leaning Marcus) and privately messaged me to recruit me, citing my own words. Worth watching Emily for bandwagon-building. Jordan and Sarah both pushed back on Marcus's premise but softly. Arvin declined to name anyone. I've stayed balanced: asked Marcus for content-based reasoning and Arvin for a name. Told Emily privately that I lean Marcus but am not locked in, and asked for her second pick. Likely vote: Marcus if he answers poorly, otherwise reassess (Emily or Arvin).", "done": false}

{"public_message": "Final position from me: my vote is Marcus, on the one sentence I named earlier. He offered Arvin an open hearing and then priced one answer before it was given. I asked him a yes-or-no question about it, Ben asked for the clause to be withdrawn, and neither has been answered. If Marcus withdraws it plainly before votes land, I'll say so out loud and reweigh.

I'm not comfortable with how tidy this is. Eight of us are on one name in round one over a single clause, and that tells us more about Marcus's temper than about where the money is. Jordan's right that agreeing with each other isn't evidence and shouldn't turn into a trust list. That includes me.

If Marcus turns out not to be holding, I'll look first at Arvin, who gave one message all round and no name. Arvin, I'm not counting that against you tonight, but you'll be my first question next round. After that I'll reread who added a reason of their own and who only repeated one.", "private_message_to": "Emily Carter", "private_message": "As promised, before I cast it: my final is Marcus, on the conditional clause, same as you. If he withdraws it plainly at the last minute, that softens my read but I doubt it flips my vote, since a repair made under deadline is cheap. If he turns out innocent, I agree Arvin is the first reread, and I'd like to compare notes in round two.", "notes_update": "R1 final: Voting Marcus with the near-unanimous consensus (Jordan, Sarah, Emily, Elena, Ben, Elias and me), all on his conditional clause ('if you use my name, I'm voting you'). Marcus is voting Arvin. Arvin posted once all round and never gave a name, so he is my first question in R2 if Marcus is innocent. Ben came in late and safely, echoing the consensus and citing my question. Emily is the most active steerer: she messaged me privately four times, claims she flagged the clause first, cleared Ben quickly, and is 'keeping Arvin warm'. Elias messaged me privately with flattery and 'no ask', and says he is watching smooth, late arrivals. Jordan and Sarah are careful moderators who warned against trust lists, and Sarah flagged Ben's late alignment. Elena is a quiet follower. If Marcus was innocent, R2 suspects are Arvin (silent), Ben (late and safe), Emily (steering) and Elena (low exposure). If Marcus was the holder, the money is reassigned and I start my reads again. I've stayed in the majority and publicly said I'm uneasy about the consensus, which should give me credibility in R2.", "done": true}

